| `secrets.scanner.record_file` | string | `.secret-scan/scanner.json` | a repo-relative path, no `..` part, that `.gitignore` ignores | `scripts/scan_secrets.py` and `scripts/install_scanner.py`, through `scripts/config_loader.py`'s `secrets.scanner.record_file` row | Moves where `make secrets-install` records the scanner's absolute path, rev and sha256, which every scan checks before it runs the program; a scanner on PATH is never run. A path git would track is exit 14 at `make secrets-install`, before any fetch. Absent, the scan writes `[using default] secrets.scanner.record_file = ".secret-scan/scanner.json"` to stderr. The record must resolve inside the project; an escaping parent or target symlink is exit 14 before installation or scan temporaries, even without git. write_record raises PathEscape before writing. | a committed file: the record names one machine's path | always |
